WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.638
Because a wrong cloud fails silently,
the kit guards the host three ways.

2
00:00:04.638 --> 00:00:09.520
First, it can build each live request
from the settings without running it,

3
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.601
so a reviewer sees the exact URL.

4
00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:15.163
Second, before the first call
it compares the Graph session's

5
00:00:15.163 --> 00:00:19.012
environment and tenant with the
settings, and refuses a mismatch.

6
00:00:19.012 --> 00:00:23.473
Third, it follows a next link only if
it's on the cloud's own Graph host,

7
00:00:23.473 --> 00:00:25.987
so the token never goes anywhere else.

8
00:00:25.987 --> 00:00:28.638
Tests cover the collector and each guard.

9
00:00:28.638 --> 00:00:31.201
And remember, the live reader was tested

10
00:00:31.201 --> 00:00:34.130
against stand-in responses,
not a live tenant.
